1
00:05:56,470 --> 00:06:02,470
14 Peaks: Nothing Is Impossible is a documentary film directed by Torquil Jones.

2
00:11:52,941 --> 00:11:58,941
In 2019, Nepalese mountain climber Nirmal “Nims” Purja set out to do the unthinkable by
climbing the world’s fourteen highest summits in less than seven months.

3
00:17:49,411 --> 00:17:55,411
(The previous record was eight years).

4
00:23:45,882 --> 00:23:51,882
He called the effort “Project Possible 14/7” and saw it as a way to
inspire others to strive for greater heights in any pursuit.

5
00:29:42,352 --> 00:29:48,352
The film follows his team as they seek to defy naysayers
and push the limits of human endurance.

6
00:35:38,823 --> 00:35:44,823
Himself, played by Nirmal Purja.

7
00:41:35,294 --> 00:41:41,294
Himself, played by Jimmy Chin.

8
00:47:31,764 --> 00:47:37,764
Himself, played by Reinhold Messner.

9
00:53:28,235 --> 00:53:34,235
Herself, played by Klára Kolouchová.

10
00:59:24,705 --> 00:59:30,705
Himself (archive footage), played by Conrad Anker.

11
01:05:21,176 --> 01:05:27,176
14 Peaks: Nothing Is Impossible is a 2021 documentary film directed by Torquil Jones, and produced by Noah Media Group, Little
Monster Films and Torquil Jones with Nirmal Purja, Jimmy Chin and Elizabeth Vasarhelyi as executive producers.

12
01:11:17,647 --> 01:11:23,647
The film follows Nepalese mountaineer Nirmal Purja and his team as they attempt to climb all
14 eight-thousander peaks within a then record time of under seven months.

13
01:17:14,117 --> 01:17:20,117
The previous record was over seven years.

14
01:23:10,588 --> 01:23:16,588
A significant portion of the footage was taken by the expedition team, while additional images and interviews were added later by the director, including interviews with Reinhold Messner
(who called the feat "a unique statement in the history of mountaineering"), and other major high-altitude mountaineers, and Purja's family (including his wife and brothers).

15
01:29:07,058 --> 01:29:13,058
The film premiered at the DOC NYC Film Festival, and was
released on Netflix on 29 November 2021.

16
01:35:03,529 --> 01:35:09,529
The film explores themes of mountain, mountaineer,
k2, mountain climbing, mountaineering.
